<section xml:id="sec-skel-hyp-more-examples">
<title>Further Examples</title>

<example xml:id="example-skel-hyp-catenary">
<title>A hanging telephone line</title>
<statement>
<p>
A telephone line hangs between two poles <m>14</m> m apart in the shape
of the catenary <m>y = 20\cosh(x/20) - 15</m>, where <m>x</m> and
<m>y</m> are measured in meters.
<ol marker="A.">
<li>
<p>
Find the slope of this curve where it meets the right pole.
</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>
Find the angle <m>\theta</m> between the line and the pole.
</p>
</li>
</ol>
</p>

<p>
<em>Solution.</em>
(A sketch of the line between the poles at <m>x = -7</m> and
<m>x = 7</m> may help.)
</p>

<sidebyside width="97%">
<image>
<latex-image>
\begin{tikzpicture}
\draw[rounded corners=8pt, draw=gray!55, thick] (0,0) rectangle (15,12);
\node[anchor=north west, text=gray!60, font=\footnotesize\itshape]
  at (0.25,11.75) {workspace};
\end{tikzpicture}
</latex-image>
<shortdescription>Blank workspace for a handwritten solution and sketch.</shortdescription>
</image>
</sidebyside>
</statement>
</example>

<example xml:id="example-skel-hyp-sinh-ln">
<title>Rewriting <m>\sinh(\ln(x))</m></title>
<statement>
<p>
Consider the function <m>f(x) = \sinh(\ln(x))</m>.
<ol marker="A.">
<li>
<p>
Express <m>f(x)</m> as a fraction of two polynomials.
</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>
Calculate <m>\dfrac{df}{dx}</m>.
</p>
</li>
</ol>
</p>

<p>
<em>Solution.</em>
</p>

<sidebyside width="97%">
<image>
<latex-image>
\begin{tikzpicture}
\draw[rounded corners=8pt, draw=gray!55, thick] (0,0) rectangle (15,10);
\node[anchor=north west, text=gray!60, font=\footnotesize\itshape]
  at (0.25,9.75) {workspace};
\end{tikzpicture}
</latex-image>
<shortdescription>Blank workspace for a handwritten solution.</shortdescription>
</image>
</sidebyside>
</statement>
</example>

<example xml:id="example-skel-hyp-double-angle">
<title>A double-angle identity</title>
<statement>
<p>
Prove that <m>\sinh(2x) = 2\sinh(x)\cosh(x)</m>.
</p>

<p>
<em>Proof (start from the definitions).</em>
</p>

